Subject: [PATCH] compose: Windows and Linux profiles claim the host CPU architecture

A page can tell the CPU family from arithmetic, such as the sign bit of
a computed NaN or Web Audio output. A Windows profile claiming x86 while
running on ARM looks like x86 Windows emulated on ARM, which
FingerprintJS flags as a virtual machine. Windows and Linux profiles
take platform.architecture from the build's CPU, and a Linux profile on
ARM reports navigator.platform "Linux aarch64". macOS profiles keep arm.

diff --git a/base/apostate/compose.cc b/base/apostate/compose.cc
index 406d4df..cbd34a6 100644
--- a/base/apostate/compose.cc
+++ b/base/apostate/compose.cc
@@ -1637,6 +1637,26 @@ std::optional<Composition> Compose(const ComposeRequest& request,
   DeriveWorkArea(composition.profile, panel_resolved,
                  &composition.limitations);
 
+  // The CPU shows through arithmetic a page can run (the sign of a computed
+  // NaN, audio rendering), so a Windows or Linux persona claims the
+  // architecture the browser actually runs on. Claiming x86 on an ARM machine
+  // reads as x86 Windows emulated on ARM, which detectors flag as a virtual
+  // machine. A macOS persona keeps arm: Intel-build Chrome under Rosetta on
+  // Apple silicon also reports arm next to an Apple GPU.
+  if (DictValue* platform = composition.profile.FindDict("platform")) {
+    const std::string* name = platform->FindString("name");
+    if (name && (*name == "Windows" || *name == "Linux")) {
+#if defined(ARCH_CPU_ARM_FAMILY)
+      platform->Set("architecture", "arm");
+      if (*name == "Linux") {
+        platform->Set("navigator_platform", "Linux aarch64");
+      }
+#else
+      platform->Set("architecture", "x86");
+#endif
+    }
+  }
+
   // A diagnostic handle, not a claim: patch 0004 reads `id` into source_id_
   // and nothing page-visible consumes it. Naming it after the root makes a
   // profile traceable back to the tuple that produced it.
